All 60 jobs finished, the pool is imported, and H1388 is now at **POOL_READY**. One problem: only the AF3 models actually carry the pS7 phosphate.

**Model counts (A1B1).** Every run has exactly the number of models it should, none with an empty file and none flagged for clashes. The import needed one workaround: the runs sit under `runs/<runner>_<variant>/`, but `residudes pool` only reads `results/<sto>/<variant>/<runner>/`. I added links from that layout to the runs and imported with `--dir`; the models were not moved.

| run | models | median ranking score | max | max ipTM | phosphate in model |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| af3, SEP | 100 | 0.944 | 0.963 | 0.939 | 100/100 |
| af3, unmodified control | 50 | 0.652 | 0.764 | 0.693 | 0/50 (intended) |
| pt2, SEP | 50 | 0.918 | 0.930 | 0.920 | **0/50** |
| bt2, SEP | 50 | 0.912 | 0.923 | 0.908 | **0/50** |
| of3, SEP | 50 | 0.585 | 0.743 | 0.669 | **0/50** |

**The phosphate.** The pt2, bt2 and of3 "SEP" models have plain SER at peptide residue 7 and no phosphorus atom. They are effectively predictions of the unmodified peptide, whatever the variant label says. pt2 and bt2 still score about 0.91–0.92, against 0.65 for the unmodified AF3 control, so their confidence does not come from the phosphate. From the logs I read I can't tell whether those three tools dropped the modification when reading the input or when writing the model.

What this means for the next stage:
- The planned gate requiring the phosphate near the binding site can only pass on AF3 SEP models.
- At results review, treat the pt2, bt2 and of3 models as unmodified.

Both points are in the dossier: the counts and the phosphate check under evidence key `pool`, plus an FYI note. Next comes QA (interface and clustering) and running the structural gates.

